# Copy to .env and fill in. `zeos-blocks run` and `zeos-blocks serve` read this file,
# from the current directory and then the project root. A variable already set in the
# environment wins over it, and a command-line flag wins over both. The names are the
# Claude SDK's own, so a shell already set up for Claude needs no .env at all.
#
# None of this is needed by the stub planner, the lint or the test suite, which is
# most of what this demonstration is. Only `--planner claude` wants a key.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Overridden by --model. Opus by default: the planner is asked for one command at a
# time with the table in front of it, and a smaller model is likelier to answer with
# prose the seat then has to shape into a command.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
